1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,336
My daughter just turned seven for the fifth time today, and she still hasn't learned to tie her shoes.

2
00:00:06,636 --> 00:00:15,876
The morning sun hits the table at the exact same angle. I reach for my coffee. It's always lukewarm.

3
00:00:16,176 --> 00:00:23,376
I kiss my wife, Sarah. Her skin is soft, but her eyes never quite focus on mine when I speak.

4
00:00:23,676 --> 00:00:31,788
Yesterday, I tried to walk out the front door. I found a solid, unyielding wall of static instead.

5
00:00:32,088 --> 00:00:40,656
Everything here is a loop. A perfect, polished loop designed to keep me from ever feeling actual, stinging pain.

6
00:00:40,956 --> 00:00:50,652
I found a remote tucked under the floorboards. One button. It labels this world as 'Package 402: Idealized Family'.

7
00:00:50,952 --> 00:00:57,624
I am not a father. I am not a husband. I am an animation meant to soothe a lonely client.

8
00:00:57,924 --> 00:01:05,436
Beyond the static, I hear a woman weeping. She is the one paying for my every single gentle smile.

9
00:01:05,736 --> 00:01:15,336
The subscription is running low. The colors are washing out. My life is literally flickering out of existence now.

10
00:01:15,636 --> 00:01:21,828
My daughter just turned seven for the last time, and I am finally allowed to stop being a memory.
